  "details": "Dynamic bones' Inert function, whether intentionally or not, had a quirk where setting it higher would make the bone travel relative to your entire avatar descriptor, and the amount of influence was based on how high the value was.\nThis meant that hair bones would clip through you or spaz out much less when set at high values, while still maintaining rotational bounce when, say, shaking your head. \nCurrently, the Immobile function of phys bones does not support this. This makes hair very hard to do properly, as it will usually go crazy when the character moves, and setting it to higher immobility causes it to stiffen up in an unwanted fashion. \nI think this could be solved one of two ways. Either adding that functionality back in, or my prefered option, having a reference object that the bone chain checks all of its simulations against to see whether it should be moving with the specified transform, or more/less. Having a slider to control how much this reference object influences the bone would be very useful in conjunction with the toggle.",
